TEXT 0 -224 Left 2 ;Second-order low-pass (series RLC, output on C): H(s) = ω0² / (s² + s ω0/Q + ω0²)\nω0 = 1/√(LC) = 31.6 krad/s (f0 ≈ 5.03 kHz) and Q = √(L/C) / R ≈ 2.1: two complex poles at −ω0/2Q ± jω0√(1 − 1/4Q²).\nStep: it overshoots (about 46 %) and rings at f0 while it settles. Bode: a peak of about Q (6.7 dB) near f0 and then −40 dB/decade; the phase goes from 0 to −180°.
